# 5. Cardinality and safe disposition

## 5.1 Exact identity invariants

5.1.1 the identity set must be exactly `TRD2-SHR-F001` through `TRD2-SHR-F020`, once each, without Gap, duplicate, Alias or extra record.

5.1.2 exact severity partition: `F001–F009=P0`; `F010–F018=P1`; `F019–F020=P2`; `P3=0`.

5.1.3 every `mergeKey` equals its `findingId`; every status is `OPEN`.

5.1.4 closure, downgrade, false-positive, duplicate, suppression or risk disposition requires a separate future root-bound authorized record and cannot edit this manifest in place.

## 5.2 Terminal

5.2.1 manifest validity does not imply subject validity. A structurally valid Findings Manifest can preserve a `REJECT` verdict.

5.2.2 safe disposition=`REJECT`; `Gate29=BLOCKED`; `Development freeze=ACTIVE`; no Materialization, Product, Git or Provider authority is created.

5.2.3 any subject-byte change makes this manifest stale and requires a new independent review; it does not transfer findings or review credit automatically.
